                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86499eed-4ed5-4460-877d-fdb88a171442",
                                                "sense_id": "f9a435d2-118d-3f68-9fdb-ecac32abcaa2",
                                                "text": "Give that lamp a good rub and see if any genies come out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25f1ced4-1e9e-3a43-97e6-c2526deecb0f",
                                        "entry_id": "c5c13bd2-8b5f-394a-8723-e4e9ead228e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A difficulty or problem."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7b0fdc2-207b-4516-badd-72a5c6a0ca52",
                                                "sense_id": "25f1ced4-1e9e-3a43-97e6-c2526deecb0f",
                                                "text": "To die, to sleep— / To sleep—perchance to dream. Ay, there's the rub! / For in that sleep of death what dreams may come, / When we have shuffled off this mortal coil, / Must give us pause"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a1e1f91-4d34-4b02-9183-3186fc2e2c22",
                                                "sense_id": "25f1ced4-1e9e-3a43-97e6-c2526deecb0f",
                                                "text": "[…] the propriety of the cabman's shelter, as it was called, hardly a stonesthrow away near Butt bridge where they might hit upon some drinkables in the shape of a milk and soda or a mineral. But how to get there was the rub."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e9220a0-c023-4508-8db9-ec9390a1a61f",
                                                "sense_id": "25f1ced4-1e9e-3a43-97e6-c2526deecb0f",
                                                "text": "'My dear Devereux, I say, you mustn't talk in that wild way. You—you talk like a ruined man!'\n'And I so comfortable!'\n'Why, to be sure, Dick, you have had some little rubs, and, maybe, your follies and your vexations; but, hang it, you are young; you can't get experience—at least, so I've found it—without paying for it. […]'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76551f4f-51a0-38b4-86bb-5809c3fb7400",
                                        "entry_id": "c5c13bd2-8b5f-394a-8723-e4e9ead228e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quip or sarcastic remark."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e631a156-186c-3f7d-b129-7778502a4c87",
